---
title: "repay_debt / unsafe_repay_debt_only (Pebble Protocol: Obligation)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_accrue: accrue_interest(CoinType, asset_borrow_index)
    q_accrue --> q_get_debt: debt_amount = debt.unsafe_debt_amount().ceil()
    q_get_debt --> q_check_full: debt_amount <= repay_amount?
    q_check_full --> q_full_repay: yes (full repay)
    q_check_full --> q_partial_repay: no (partial repay)
    q_full_repay --> q_clear: debt.cleared()
    q_clear --> q_calc_residual: residual = repay_amount - debt_amount
    q_calc_residual --> q_check_has_debt: debt.has_debt()?
    q_partial_repay --> q_decrease: debt.unsafe_decrease(repay_amount)
    q_decrease --> q_no_residual: residual = 0
    q_no_residual --> q_check_has_debt
    q_check_has_debt --> q_remove: no debt remaining
    q_remove --> q_wit_remove: wit_table::remove(debts, name)
    q_wit_remove --> [*]: return residual
    q_check_has_debt --> q_keep: debt remaining
    q_keep --> [*]: return residual

    note right of q_full_repay
        INV-001: debt.ceil() used for full repay (borrower may overpay by dust)
        INV-002: cleared debt sets amount to zero
        INV-003: zero-debt entries removed from obligation
    end note

    note right of q_decrease
        INV-004: partial repay reduces debt by exact amount
        INV-005: unsafe_decrease requires prior interest accrual
    end note
